'''11 Carrer Balisca''' is a 40-storey multi-tenant office tower at 11 Carrer Balisca in the [[Districte Financer (Original, Sant Cristòfor)|Districte Financer]] of [[Original (ciutat)|Original]], [[Sant Cristòfor]], [[Balboa]]. Completed in 2002, the tower is one of the prominent commercial buildings on the Sant Cristòfor waterfront. At 162 metres (531 ft), it is among the taller office towers in the Districte Financer.

== Architecture ==

11 Carrer Balisca is a large modern office tower with a broad, rectangular massing and a restrained late-modernist design. The façade is almost entirely clad in blue-green curtain-wall glass, arranged in a tight grid of horizontal floor bands and narrow vertical mullions. The most distinctive feature is a strong vertical strip along one side, where pale metal or concrete fins rise continuously up the façade, giving the otherwise wide, boxy tower a more slender appearance and emphasising its height. A slightly projecting vertical section near the corner adds additional depth and breaks up the flat glass surfaces.

The building has a nearly rectangular floor plate with large, efficient office floors suited to corporate tenants. The roof is flat with minimal visible mechanical equipment. A landscaped plaza with tropical greenery surrounds the base.

